"IAB4","Careers","Broad content encompassing professional development, workforce trends, and the job market. Includes labor market analysis, industry-specific hiring trends in India, workplace culture, salary benchmarks, and professional upskilling resources across both private and public sectors."
"IAB4-1","Career Planning","Strategic content for long-term professional growth. Includes advice on skill development, choosing career paths in growing sectors (like AI, Data Science, or Green Energy), mentorship, networking, and transitions between industries or roles."
"IAB4-2","College","Information related to higher education as a gateway to careers. Covers entrance exams (JEE, NEET, CAT, GATE), campus placement preparation, university selection, undergraduate/postgraduate degree programs, and the transition from academic life to corporate environments."
"IAB4-3","Financial Aid","Content concerning funding for higher education and professional training. Includes information on education loans (from banks like SBI, HDFC), interest subsidies, government grants, and financial planning for expensive professional courses or overseas studies."
"IAB4-4","Job Fairs","Coverage of recruitment events, campus placement drives, and job melas. Focuses on the ecosystem of offline and digital hiring events, job expos organized by universities, and industry-specific hiring conclaves where candidates interact directly with recruiters."
"IAB4-5","Job Search","Practical guidance and platforms for finding employment. Covers popular Indian job portals (Naukri, LinkedIn, Indeed), networking strategies, headhunting agencies, and tips for navigating the recruitment process in a competitive market."
"IAB4-6","Resume Writing/Advice","Content on creating impactful professional profiles. Includes advice on crafting resumes, CV formats, LinkedIn profile optimization, cover letter writing, and building portfolios that stand out in Indian applicant tracking systems (ATS)."
"IAB4-7","Nursing","Specialized content regarding careers in the healthcare and nursing sector. Covers nursing degree programs (B.Sc. Nursing), entrance examinations, career paths in hospitals and clinics, medical tourism, and international nursing opportunities for Indian professionals."
"IAB4-8","Scholarships","Information on merit-based and need-based financial awards. Covers government-funded scholarships (like AICTE or UGC grants), private corporate scholarships, and fellowships for students pursuing professional or technical education in India."
"IAB4-9","Telecommuting","Information on remote work, hybrid models, and digital nomadism. Covers the rise of WFH (Work From Home) culture in India’s IT/ITeS sector, tools for distributed teams, digital productivity, and legal/policy aspects of remote employment."
"IAB4-10","Government Jobs","Information regarding public sector employment. Highly specific to the Indian context, covering UPSC (Civil Services), SSC (Staff Selection Commission), Banking (IBPS/SBI PO), Railways, and State Public Service Commissions. Includes exam notifications, preparation tips, and eligibility criteria."
"IAB4-11","Career Advice","General professional guidance and soft-skills development. Includes articles on workplace communication, conflict resolution, leadership training, preparing for group discussions and personal interviews (GD/PI), and general career motivation."
"IAB5","Education","Comprehensive coverage of the Indian education system, encompassing primary schooling, higher education, and lifelong learning. Includes policies like the National Education Policy (NEP 2020), the Right to Education (RTE) Act, digital literacy, the massive Indian EdTech ecosystem, and both traditional classroom and online pedagogies."
"IAB5-1","7-12 Education","Content focused on secondary and higher secondary schooling in India (Classes 7 to 12). Covers major educational boards (CBSE, ICSE, and various State Boards), board examination preparation, curriculum updates, foundational coaching for competitive exams (JEE, NEET), and STEM vs. Commerce stream selections."
"IAB5-2","Adult Education","Information regarding continuing education for mature learners. Covers adult literacy programs, the Skill India initiative, vocational training, night schools, polytechnic diplomas, and professional upskilling courses designed for workforce integration and non-traditional students."
"IAB5-3","Art History","Study of historical visual arts, architecture, and cultural artifacts. In the Indian context, this covers academic curriculum focused on ancient Indian architecture (Dravidian and Nagara styles), Mughal and Rajput paintings, classical antiquity, and preparation for humanities and fine arts degrees."
"IAB5-4","College Administration","Content related to the management and governance of higher education institutions. Covers regulatory bodies like the University Grants Commission (UGC), AICTE, and the Medical Council of India (MCI/NMC), NAAC accreditation processes, institutional funding, and academic policy implementation."
"IAB5-5","College Life","Discussions on the campus culture and student experience in Indian universities. Covers life at premier institutes (IITs, NITs, IIMs, Delhi University), hostel living, cultural fests (like IIT Bombay's Mood Indigo), student unions, college societies, and the transition from school to independent college life."
"IAB5-6","Distance Learning","Content concerning remote education and correspondence courses. Highlights India's open universities (such as IGNOU and YCMOU), online degree programs, massive open online courses (MOOCs like SWAYAM), and the rapid expansion of virtual classrooms and EdTech platforms bridging the rural-urban divide."
"IAB5-7","English as a 2nd Language","Information focused on English language acquisition for non-native speakers. Covers spoken English coaching centers, vernacular-to-English transition strategies, and preparation for international proficiency tests (IELTS, TOEFL, PTE) commonly required for overseas education and global employment."
"IAB5-8","Language Learning","Content regarding the study of regional and foreign languages. Covers learning indigenous Indian languages (Hindi, Tamil, Sanskrit, Bengali, etc.) as well as acquiring global languages (French, German, Spanish) through institutions like the Goethe-Institut (Max Mueller Bhavan) or the Alliance Française."
"IAB5-9","Graduate School","Information concerning postgraduate studies and research programs. Covers Master's degrees (M.Tech, MA, M.Sc), Ph.D. research fellowships (UGC-NET, JRF), the GATE examination, academic publishing, thesis defense, and admissions into premier Indian research institutions like IISc and TIFR."
"IAB5-10","Homeschooling","Content focused on alternative education models outside traditional formal schooling. Covers the niche but growing urban Indian trend of unschooling, customized home curriculums, and utilizing the National Institute of Open Schooling (NIOS) board for standardized testing and certification."
"IAB5-11","Homework/Study Tips","Practical guidance for academic success and exam preparation. Covers revision techniques, time management for board exams, rote learning vs. conceptual understanding, memory aids (mnemonics), creating study timetables, and utilizing online doubt-solving apps and peer study groups."
"IAB5-12","K-6 Educators","Resources and content tailored for primary school teachers and early childhood education. Covers foundational literacy and numeracy (FLN), Montessori and Waldorf pedagogies, Anganwadi curriculum, classroom management, and child psychology for students from Kindergarten through 6th grade."
"IAB5-13","Private School","Information regarding independent, unaided, and fee-charging schools. Covers premium international boards (IB, IGCSE), prestigious Indian boarding schools (like The Doon School, Mayo College), elite day schools, school fee structures, and the competitive nursery admission process in metropolitan cities."
"IAB5-14","Special Education","Content focused on inclusive education for students with specific learning or physical needs. Covers learning disabilities (Dyslexia, ADHD, Autism spectrum), individualized education programs (IEPs), Guidelines by the Rehabilitation Council of India (RCI), and training for special educators."
"IAB5-15","Studying Business","Information concerning commerce, finance, and management education. Covers degrees like B.Com and BBA, professional certifications (Chartered Accountancy - CA, Company Secretary - CS), and rigorous preparation for Indian MBA entrance exams (CAT, XAT, NMAT) targeting tier-1 B-schools."
"IAB6","Family & Parenting","Broad content focusing on domestic life, child-rearing, and household dynamics. In the Indian context, this encompasses the transition from traditional multi-generational joint families to urban nuclear setups, cultural values (sanskar), kinship networks, work-life balance for working parents, and managing relationships across generations."
"IAB6-1","Adoption","Content related to the legal, social, and emotional processes of adopting children. Covers Indian adoption regulations under CARA (Central Adoption Resource Authority), the Hindu Adoptions and Maintenance Act (HAMA), the Juvenile Justice Act, navigating complex legal paperwork, overcoming social stigmas, and foster care."
"IAB6-2","Babies and Toddlers","Information regarding infant care and early childhood development (ages 0-3). Includes pediatric health, vaccination schedules (BCG, Polio, DPT), traditional Indian baby care practices (maalish/mustard oil massage), cultural ceremonies (Mundan, Annaprashan), sleep training, weaning, and infant nutrition (Cerelac, homemade purees)."
"IAB6-3","Daycare/Pre School","Content focused on early childhood care and education (ECCE) for working families. Covers the booming Indian playschool sector (such as Kidzee, EuroKids), government Anganwadi centers, corporate creches, Montessori methodologies, and the logistical challenges of hiring trusted domestic nannies (ayahs)."
"IAB6-4","Family Internet","Guidance on digital safety, broadband usage, and technology consumption within the household. Covers digital parenting, setting screen time limits, parental control software, cyberbullying awareness, safe online gaming environments, family WhatsApp groups, and digital literacy for senior citizens."
"IAB6-5","Parenting - K-6 Kids","Advice on raising primary school-aged children (approx. ages 5-11). Covers managing school homework, the reliance on private tuitions, balancing academics with extracurriculars, child nutrition (health drinks, tiffin box recipes), behavioral discipline, and imparting cultural/moral stories (Panchatantra, mythology)."
"IAB6-6","Parenting teens","Content navigating adolescence, puberty, and young adulthood. In India, this heavily features managing immense academic stress (Class 10/12 board exams, JEE/NEET coaching pressure), addressing the generation gap, tackling peer pressure, teenage rebellion, and fostering open conversations about mental health and social media addiction."
"IAB6-7","Pregnancy","Information on maternal health, obstetrics, and the journey from conception to childbirth. Covers prenatal care, traditional Indian pregnancy customs (Godh Bharai/baby shower, postpartum confinement diets like panjiri and ghee), maternity leave laws, sonography regulations (PCPNDT Act), and newborn nursing."
"IAB6-8","Special Needs Kids","Resources for parenting children with physical, developmental, or learning disabilities. Covers navigating the Indian inclusive education system, seeking specialized therapies (speech, occupational), understanding neurodivergence (Autism spectrum, ADHD, Dyslexia), the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, and localized parent support networks."
"IAB6-9","Eldercare","Content focused on geriatric health, senior citizen welfare, and supporting aging parents. Discusses the strong Indian cultural ethos of filial duty (Shravan Kumar ideal), home healthcare nursing, managing chronic illnesses (diabetes, dementia), the rise of premium assisted living and retirement communities, and Ayushman Bharat senior schemes."
"IAB7","Health & Fitness","Broad coverage of physical and mental well-being, preventative healthcare, and medical treatments. In India, this spans modern allopathic medicine (Apollo, Fortis), traditional AYUSH practices (Ayurveda, Yoga, Unani, Siddha, Homeopathy), fitness trends, government health schemes (Ayushman Bharat, CGHS), and generic pharmaceutical availability (Jan Aushadhi)."
"IAB7-1","Exercise","Content focused on physical workouts and fitness regimens. Covers the Indian gym culture (Cult.fit, Gold's Gym), indigenous practices like Surya Namaskar and Akhara wrestling (Pehlwani), marathon training in tier-1 cities, Zumba, and general home workout trends."
"IAB7-2","A.D.D.","Information on Attention Deficit Disorder (ADHD) management. Focuses on neurodivergence in the Indian context, destigmatizing pediatric mental health, specialized educational accommodations, pediatric psychiatry, and behavioral therapy available in metropolitan cities."
"IAB7-3","AIDS/HIV","Content regarding HIV prevention, treatment, and living with AIDS. Covers the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO) guidelines, ART (Antiretroviral Therapy) centers in India, breaking rural stigmas, NGOs working in high-risk group rehabilitation, and sexual health awareness."
"IAB7-4","Allergies","Information on managing hypersensitivity and allergic reactions. Covers common Indian allergens like pollen, dust mites, and pollution-induced rhinitis (especially in Delhi NCR), food allergies (lactose, peanut), antihistamine medications, and traditional dietary avoidances."
"IAB7-5","Alternative Medicine","Content dedicated to non-allopathic healing practices. Deeply rooted in India via the AYUSH ministry, covering Ayurvedic doshas (Vata, Pitta, Kapha), Panchakarma therapy, Homeopathy remedies (Arnica, Nux Vomica), Siddha medicine in Tamil Nadu, and Naturopathy."
"IAB7-6","Arthritis","Information on joint inflammation and musculoskeletal pain. Covers osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis prevalent among the Indian elderly demographic, pain management via allopathic analgesics, physiotherapies, and Ayurvedic treatments like Shallaki and joint massages."
"IAB7-7","Asthma","Content regarding chronic respiratory conditions. Highly relevant in India due to urban air pollution (high AQI) and crop stubble burning. Covers asthma inhalers (Cipla), nebulization, pediatric asthma, pulmonary function tests, and breathing exercises like Pranayama."
"IAB7-8","Autism/PDD","Resources for Autism Spectrum Disorder and Pervasive Developmental Disorders. Covers early diagnostic centers in India, occupational and speech therapy, navigating the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, and breaking societal taboos around neurodivergence."
"IAB7-9","Bipolar Disorder","Information on managing manic-depressive illness. Focuses on psychiatric care, mood stabilizers, the role of family support in the Indian joint family structure, the Mental Healthcare Act 2017, and destigmatizing severe mental health conditions."
"IAB7-10","Brain Tumor","Content covering neuro-oncology and brain cancer treatments. Details advanced neurosurgery options at premier Indian institutes (NIMHANS, AIIMS), radiation therapy, chemotherapy protocols, diagnostic MRIs, and patient rehabilitation."
"IAB7-11","Cancer","Comprehensive oncology resources. Covers breast, cervical, and oral cancers (highly prevalent in India due to tobacco/gutka consumption). Includes treatment protocols at Tata Memorial Hospital, chemotherapy, radiation, generic cancer drugs, and palliative care."
"IAB7-12","Cholesterol","Information on managing lipid levels and cardiovascular risk. Covers dietary shifts away from trans-fats and excessive ghee, statin medications, lipid profile blood tests (PathKind, Dr. Lal PathLabs), and lifestyle interventions for the Indian demographic."
"IAB7-13","Chronic Fatigue Syndrome","Content on long-term disabling fatigue (Myalgic Encephalomyelitis). Discusses diagnostic challenges in India, the impact on corporate workforce productivity, symptom management, and distinguishing CFS from general nutritional deficiencies like Vitamin D/B12."
"IAB7-14","Chronic Pain","Information on long-term pain management. Covers neuropathic pain, slipped discs, and fibromyalgia. Includes Indian pain clinics, alternative acupuncture, ergonomic corrections for IT professionals, and restrictions on opioid analgesics in India."
"IAB7-15","Cold & Flu","Guidance on seasonal viral infections. Highly relevant during the Indian monsoon and winter shifts. Covers OTC medicines (Crocin, Dolo-650, Cheston Cold), traditional Indian home remedies (kadha, haldi doodh/turmeric milk), and influenza vaccinations."
"IAB7-16","Deafness","Resources for hearing loss and audiology. Covers hearing aids, cochlear implants under government schemes (ADIP), learning Indian Sign Language (ISL), and accessible infrastructure for the hearing impaired in educational institutions."
"IAB7-17","Dental Care","Information on oral hygiene and dentistry. Covers pediatric dentistry, orthodontics (braces/aligners like toothsi), root canal treatments, periodontics, scaling, and the booming Indian cosmetic dentistry and dental tourism sector."
"IAB7-18","Depression","Content concerning major depressive disorder. Discusses the growing awareness of clinical depression in India, accessible tele-psychiatry platforms (Practo, Wysa), destigmatizing seeking therapy, anti-depressants, and suicide prevention helplines (AASRA)."
"IAB7-19","Dermatology","Information on skin, hair, and nail health. Covers common Indian skin concerns like hyperpigmentation, fungal infections (due to humid climate), acne treatments, hair loss solutions (minoxidil), and the shift towards clinical derma-skincare brands."
"IAB7-20","Diabetes","Comprehensive content on metabolic disease management. Highly critical as India is often termed the 'Diabetes Capital of the World.' Covers Type 2 diabetes, HbA1c testing, insulin administration, glucometers, dietary control (low glycemic index Indian foods), and diabetic retinopathy."
"IAB7-21","Epilepsy","Information on neurological seizure disorders. Covers anti-epileptic drug therapy, EEG diagnostics, addressing rural Indian superstitions surrounding seizures, and managing workplace/school environments for epileptic patients."
"IAB7-22","GERD/Acid Reflux","Guidance on gastroesophageal reflux disease. Common in India due to spicy, oily diets and irregular eating habits. Covers antacids (Gelusil, Digene), proton pump inhibitors (Pantocid), endoscopy, and dietary modifications like reducing chillies and caffeine."
"IAB7-23","Headaches/Migraines","Information on tension headaches and severe migraines. Covers trigger identification (sunlight, stress, skipped meals), OTC pain relievers (Saridon, Disprin), prescription triptans, and Ayurvedic stress-relief balms (Zandu Balm, Amrutanjan)."
"IAB7-24","Heart Disease","Content on cardiovascular health and cardiology. Covers the high incidence of early-onset coronary artery disease in Indians, ECG/Echo diagnostics, angioplasty, bypass surgery (CABG) at hospitals like Medanta, hypertension, and heart-healthy cooking oils."
"IAB7-25","Herbs for Health","Information on botanical and herbal remedies. Deeply integrated into the Indian lifestyle, covering medicinal plants like Ashwagandha (stress), Tulsi (immunity), Neem (antibacterial), Giloy, and the commercial market for herbal supplements (Himalaya, Patanjali)."
"IAB7-26","Holistic Healing","Content regarding whole-body wellness approaches. Covers the integration of mind, body, and spirit through practices like Vipassana meditation, Reiki, Chakra healing, Isha Foundation programs, and wellness retreats in Rishikesh and Kerala."
"IAB7-27","IBS/Crohn's Disease","Information on inflammatory and irritable bowel conditions. Covers managing digestive distress, tailored Indian diets (reducing complex lentils/dairy), colonoscopy diagnostics, gastroenterology, and gut microbiome health (probiotics/curd)."
"IAB7-28","Incest/Abuse Support","Resources for survivors of domestic violence and sexual abuse. Covers legal protections under the POCSO and Domestic Violence Acts, NGO helplines (Snehalaya, Majlis), trauma counseling, and navigating the Indian socio-legal justice system safely."
"IAB7-29","Incontinence","Information on loss of bladder or bowel control. Discusses geriatric care, the growing adult diaper market in India (Friends, KareIn), pelvic floor exercises (Kegels), urology consultations, and breaking the embarrassment surrounding the condition."
"IAB7-30","Infertility","Content regarding reproductive challenges and assisted conception. Covers the booming Indian IVF and surrogacy sector (Nova IVF, Indira IVF), the ART (Regulation) Act, dealing with societal pressures in Indian families, PCOS-related infertility, and semen analysis."
"IAB7-31","Men's Health","Information specific to male physical and mental wellness. Covers prostate health, male pattern baldness (androgenetic alopecia), erectile dysfunction, fitness supplements, and breaking the 'macho' stereotype to encourage men seeking mental health therapy."
"IAB7-32","Nutrition","Content focused on dietetics and healthy eating. Covers Indian macronutrient tracking, balancing vegetarian diets with adequate protein (paneer, soya, lentils), fortified foods, FSSAI regulations, and combating both malnutrition and urban obesity."
"IAB7-33","Orthopedics","Information on the musculoskeletal system. Covers bone health, Vitamin D/Calcium deficiencies widespread in India, joint replacements (knee/hip), spine surgeries, osteoporosis management, and sports injuries rehabilitation."
"IAB7-34","Panic/Anxiety Disorders","Content on managing severe anxiety and panic attacks. Discusses identifying triggers, cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT), anxiolytic medications, breathing techniques, and dealing with academic/corporate performance anxiety in India."
"IAB7-35","Pediatrics","Information regarding infant and child healthcare. Covers the Indian Academy of Pediatrics (IAP) immunization schedules, growth charting, childhood obesity, treating recurrent monsoon fevers (dengue, malaria), and pediatric nutrition."
"IAB7-36","Physical Therapy","Content on physiotherapy and rehabilitation. Covers post-operative care, neuro-rehabilitation, sports physiotherapy, ergonomic postural corrections for IT workers, and traditional Indian bone-setting practices transitioning to clinical physio."
"IAB7-37","Psychology/Psychiatry","Broad mental health professional resources. Covers clinical diagnosis, the DSM-5/ICD-11 frameworks, differences between psychologists and psychiatrists, the Mental Health Care Act of India, and the rising availability of online therapy platforms."
"IAB7-38","Senior Health","Information focused on geriatric care. Covers age-related ailments, fall prevention, managing multiple chronic medications (polypharmacy), dementia/Alzheimer's care, and comprehensive senior citizen health check-up packages in Indian diagnostic labs."
"IAB7-39","Sexuality","Content on sexual health, orientation, and education. Covers navigating sex education in India, safe sex practices, contraceptives (condoms, i-Pill), STD prevention, and the evolving discourse around LGBTQ+ health and rights post-Section 377 reading down."
"IAB7-40","Sleep Disorders","Information on insomnia, sleep apnea, and rest issues. Covers the impact of modern urban lifestyles, CPAP machines for obstructive sleep apnea (common due to obesity), sleep hygiene, and melatonin supplements in the Indian market."
"IAB7-41","Smoking Cessation","Guidance on quitting tobacco use. Highly relevant given the massive consumption of bidis, cigarettes, and smokeless tobacco (Gutka, Khaini) in India. Covers nicotine replacement therapy (NRT gums like Nicotex), national quitline services, and oral cancer risks."
"IAB7-42","Substance Abuse","Information on addiction recovery and rehabilitation. Covers de-addiction centers (Nasha Mukti Kendras), managing alcohol dependency, tackling the opioid/synthetic drug crisis (e.g., in Punjab), and counseling support groups like AA."
"IAB7-43","Thyroid Disease","Content regarding hypo- and hyper-thyroidism. Highly prevalent in Indian women. Covers TSH/T3/T4 blood tests, levothyroxine daily dosages (Thyronorm), dietary iodine, and managing weight fluctuations associated with thyroid imbalances."
"IAB7-44","Weight Loss","Information on obesity management and slimming. Covers diet plans (Keto, Intermittent Fasting), bariatric surgery, fitness apps (HealthifyMe), culturally adapted low-calorie Indian recipes, and breaking away from unregulated 'slimming pills'."
"IAB7-45","Women's Health","Comprehensive content on female-specific healthcare. Covers menstrual hygiene (sanitary pads, cups), PCOD/PCOS (highly prevalent in India), gynecology, menopause management, maternal mortality reduction, and breast/cervical cancer screenings."
"IAB8","Food & Drink","Comprehensive coverage of gastronomy, beverages, and culinary culture. In India, this spans diverse regional cuisines, street food culture, home cooking (ghar ka khana), the booming food delivery ecosystem (Zomato, Swiggy), FMCG food products, grocery commerce (Zepto, Blinkit), and culinary festivals."
"IAB8-1","American Cuisine","Content regarding US-origin food adapted to the Indian market. Covers the massive fast-food franchise ecosystem (McDonald's, Burger King, KFC), gourmet burger cafes in tier-1 cities, hot dogs, fried chicken, and the integration of localized variants like the McAloo Tikki."
"IAB8-2","Barbecues & Grilling","Information on grilled, roasted, and smoked foods. In the Indian context, this heavily features Tandoori cooking, live grill buffets (like Barbeque Nation, Absolute Barbecues), seekh kebabs, paneer tikka, charcoal grilling, and marinades using mustard oil and hung curd."
"IAB8-3","Cajun/Creole","Content focused on Louisianan and Southern US cuisine. While a niche segment in India, it covers specialized continental restaurants in metropolitan areas offering jambalaya, gumbo, cajun-spiced potato wedges, and blackened fish."
"IAB8-4","Chinese Cuisine","Information on the immensely popular 'Desi Chinese' or Indo-Chinese food culture. Covers street-side wok cooking, Hakka noodles, Gobi Manchurian, Schezwan fried rice, sweet corn soup, momos, and premium authentic Pan-Asian dining experiences in India."
"IAB8-5","Cocktails/Beer","Content concerning alcoholic beverages, mixology, and pub culture. Covers the Indian craft beer revolution (Bira 91, Toit), commercial lagers (Kingfisher), restobars, gin-and-tonic trends using Indian craft gins (Greater Than, Stranger & Sons), and nightlife drinking culture."
"IAB8-6","Coffee/Tea","Information on cafe culture and traditional hot beverages. Deeply ingrained in Indian daily life, covering street-side 'tapri' Masala Chai, South Indian filter coffee (kaapi) in brass tumblers, premium estate teas (Darjeeling, Assam), and the modern cafe chain ecosystem (Third Wave, Blue Tokai)."
"IAB8-7","Cuisine-Specific","Content dedicated to regional and traditional cuisines. Represents the vast Indian culinary diversity, including Punjabi dhabas (makki ki roti, butter chicken), Chettinad spices, Bengali seafood and mustard curries, Gujarati thalis, Awadhi biryanis, and Goan vindaloo."
"IAB8-8","Desserts & Baking","Information on sweets, confectionery, and baked goods. Covers traditional Indian mithai (Gulab Jamun, Kaju Katli, Rasgulla, Jalebi) highly sought after during Diwali and weddings, as well as the booming urban home-baking trend, patisseries, eggless cakes, and artisanal chocolates."
"IAB8-9","Dining Out","Content focused on restaurant discovery and eating out. Covers food reviews, cloud kitchens, fine dining, family restaurants, street food hubs (like Chandni Chowk or Khao Gali), table reservation platforms (Dineout, EazyDiner), and weekend culinary outings."
"IAB8-10","Food Allergies","Guidance on navigating dietary restrictions and hypersensitivities. Covers the growing awareness in India regarding celiac disease (gluten-free flours like ragi and besan replacing wheat), lactose intolerance, peanut allergies, and cross-contamination in commercial kitchens."
"IAB8-11","French Cuisine","Information on classic French culinary techniques and gastronomy. Focuses on premium European dining in major Indian cities, featuring authentic boulangeries, croissants, macarons, artisanal cheeses, and high-end culinary plating."
"IAB8-12","Health/Lowfat Cooking","Content regarding nutritious, calorie-conscious, and holistic eating. Covers the resurgence of Indian superfoods and millets (jowar, bajra, amaranth), cold-pressed oils, air-frying recipes, the Sattvic diet, keto-friendly Indian meals, and reducing refined sugar and trans-fats."
"IAB8-13","Italian Cuisine","Information on pasta, pizza, and Mediterranean cooking. Extremely popular in India, ranging from localized street-side sweet-corn pizzas to authentic Neapolitan wood-fired pizzerias, artisanal pasta making, risottos, and the widespread use of oregano and chili flakes."
"IAB8-14","Japanese Cuisine","Content concerning sushi, ramen, and Japanese gastronomy. A rapidly growing trend among urban Indian millennials, covering izakayas, tempura, matcha-flavored desserts, and the adaptation of vegetarian sushi rolls (using paneer or avocado)."
"IAB8-15","Mexican Cuisine","Information on Tex-Mex and traditional Mexican food. Highly compatible with the Indian palate due to shared flavor profiles (cumin, chili, coriander). Covers tacos, nachos with salsa and queso, burritos, fajitas, and guacamole."
"IAB8-16","Vegan","Content focused on strictly plant-based diets excluding all animal products. A growing urban lifestyle choice in India, covering dairy alternatives (almond/oat/soy milk), plant-based mock meats (GoodDot, Blue Tribe), vegan baking, and replacing traditional ghee with cold-pressed plant oils."
"IAB8-17","Vegetarian","Information concerning meat-free diets. Deeply rooted in Indian culture and religion. Covers 'Shudh Shakahari' (pure veg) dining, Jain food protocols (no onion, garlic, or root vegetables), plant-protein sources (paneer, dal, soya chunks), and expansive vegetarian thalis."
"IAB8-18","Wine","Content regarding viticulture, wine tasting, and pairings. Covers the emerging Indian wine industry centered in Nashik (Sula Vineyards, Fratelli, Grover Zampa), understanding grape varietals (Shiraz, Chenin Blanc), wine tourism, and pairing wines with spicy Indian food."
"IAB11","Law, Government & Politics","Content covering Indian legislation, parliamentary affairs, governmental structures, political processes, civic duties, public policy, the Indian judicial system, and public administration."
"IAB11-1","Immigration","Information regarding Indian visas, citizenship, border control, Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) cards, NRI status, FRRO regulations, passports, deportation, and policies affecting migrants and expats."
"IAB11-2","Legal Issues","Topics related to Indian civil and criminal law (including BNS/IPC), lawsuits, litigation, legal advice, constitutional rights, Supreme Court and High Court rulings, judicial proceedings, and advocate services."
"IAB11-3","Indian Government Resources","Official public services, central and state agency information, government schemes (Yojanas), citizen services, compliance, and official portals like UIDAI (Aadhaar), the Income Tax Department, EPFO, and RTO."
"IAB11-4","Politics","Content about Indian political campaigns, Lok Sabha and Vidhan Sabha elections, voting, political parties, domestic and foreign policy, parliamentary debates, governmental leadership, and regional political discourse."
"IAB11-5","Commentary","Opinion pieces, Indian political analysis, editorials, op-eds, ideological debates, subjective perspectives, and critical reviews of current national events, government policies, and societal issues."
"IAB12","News","General journalistic reporting, breaking news, current events, press releases, journalism, and broad coverage of daily events across various domains and geographic locations."
"IAB12-1","International News","Global current events, foreign affairs, international relations, global conflicts, geopolitics, cross-border treaties, and news happening outside the reader's home country."
"IAB12-2","National News","Domestic current events, country-wide headlines, federal government updates, nationwide trends, internal crises, and major stories affecting the entire nation."
"IAB12-3","Local News","Regional and municipal updates, city council news, local weather, community events, neighborhood reporting, state-level politics, and stories relevant to a specific city or county."
"IAB13","Personal Finance","Managing individual wealth, household budgeting, saving money, personal banking, building net worth, financial literacy, and broad economic decision-making for individuals."
"IAB13-1","Beginning Investing","Introductory resources for novice investors, basics of the stock market, investing 101, building a starter portfolio, compound interest, and fundamental investment strategies."
"IAB13-2","Credit/Debt & Loans","Managing credit scores, credit cards, mortgages, student loans, auto financing, debt consolidation, interest rates, bankruptcy, and borrowing money responsibly."
"IAB13-3","Financial News","Updates on global markets, economic indicators, corporate earnings reports, Wall Street trends, central bank policies, inflation, macroeconomics, and business journalism."
"IAB13-4","Financial Planning","Long-term wealth management, setting financial goals, estate planning, budgeting strategies, working with financial advisors, trust funds, and holistic wealth mapping."
"IAB13-5","Hedge Fund","Advanced alternative investments, institutional investing, pooled capital, private equity, short selling, leveraged funds, accredited investors, and high-net-worth strategies."
"IAB13-6","Insurance","Coverage policies for health, auto, life, home, and property. Risk management, monthly premiums, deductibles, claims processes, annuities, and finding insurance quotes."
"IAB13-7","Investing","Broad investment strategies, portfolio diversification, asset allocation, capital markets, wealth generation, passive income, and general trading across multiple asset classes."
"IAB13-8","Mutual Funds","Professionally managed investment portfolios, index funds, ETFs (Exchange Traded Funds), pooled money for investing in stocks and bonds, and comparing fund performance and expense ratios."
"IAB13-9","Options","Derivatives trading, call and put options, strike prices, expiration dates, hedging strategies, implied volatility, and advanced speculative trading in the financial markets."
"IAB13-10","Retirement Planning","Preparing financially for post-career life, 401(k) plans, IRAs, Roth IRAs, pensions, social security benefits, retirement savings goals, and managing senior living expenses."
"IAB13-11","Stocks","Equities trading, buying and selling company shares, stock market analysis, dividend investing, stock tickers, day trading, blue-chip companies, and public company valuations."
"IAB13-12","Tax Planning","Minimizing tax liabilities, income tax preparation, filing returns, tax deductions, capital gains taxes, corporate taxes, CPA services, audit prevention, and IRS compliance strategies."
"IAB23","Religion & Spirituality","Content covering global belief systems, faith, theology, divine worship, spiritual growth, sacred texts, religious institutions, morality, philosophy of religion, inner peace, and practices connecting to a higher power."
"IAB23-1","Alternative Religions","Information on non-mainstream or emerging belief systems, New Age movements, esoteric traditions, occult practices, syncretic religions, spiritualism, Unitarian Universalism, Scientology, and indigenous belief systems."
"IAB23-2","Atheism/Agnosticism","Topics related to secularism, freethinking, humanism, non-belief, skepticism, rationality, scientific naturalism, disbelief in deities, secular ethics, and philosophical inquiries questioning the existence of a higher power."
"IAB23-3","Buddhism","Content focused on the teachings of Siddhartha Gautama (the Buddha), Dharma, Sangha, Zen, Theravada, Mahayana, Tibetan practices, mindfulness, meditation, karma, nirvana, the Four Noble Truths, and the Eightfold Path."
"IAB23-4","Catholicism","Information specifically about the Roman Catholic Church, the Pope, the Vatican, sacraments, the Holy Mass, Holy Communion, canonization of saints, the Virgin Mary, priesthood, canon law, and Catholic liturgy."
"IAB23-5","Christianity","Broad coverage of the Christian faith including Protestantism, Eastern Orthodox, and Evangelical denominations. Topics include Jesus Christ, the Bible (Old and New Testaments), the Gospel, salvation, baptism, church services, and Christian theology."
"IAB23-6","Hinduism","Content detailing Sanatana Dharma, core texts (Vedas, Upanishads, Bhagavad Gita), deities (Shiva, Vishnu, Krishna, Devi), concepts of karma, dharma, moksha, reincarnation, puja, temple rituals, yoga philosophy, and major festivals like Diwali."
"IAB23-7","Islam","Topics covering the Islamic faith, teachings of Prophet Muhammad, the Quran, Hadith, Sunnah, the Five Pillars of Islam, mosques, Ramadan fasting, the Hajj pilgrimage to Mecca, Sharia, and both Sunni and Shia traditions."
"IAB23-8","Judaism","Content regarding the Jewish faith, the Torah, Tanakh, Talmud, synagogues, rabbis, Jewish traditions, kosher dietary laws, the Sabbath (Shabbat), and major holidays like Passover, Yom Kippur, and Hanukkah across Orthodox, Conservative, and Reform branches."
"IAB23-9","Latter-Day Saints","Information on Mormonism and the LDS Church, including the Book of Mormon, teachings of Joseph Smith and Brigham Young, prophetic revelation, temple ordinances, missionary work, and LDS theology."
"IAB23-10","Pagan/Wiccan","Content covering earth-based and nature-centric religions, Neopaganism, Wicca, witchcraft, polytheism, druidry, magick, goddess worship, covens, and rituals celebrating natural cycles like solstices and equinoxes."
